~ s1_goal
Cyrus Rowe: The vault. And not a soul the wiser.
=> END

~ s2_goal
Cyrus Rowe: Past the statue, past the hound, past the captain himself. Not bad.
=> END

~ s3_start
Enfina Moonwish: You came back for me.
Cyrus Rowe: Stay close, and stay behind me. Where I hide, you hide.
=> END

~ s3_goal
Enfina Moonwish: We're out. I owe you one.
Cyrus Rowe: You owe me several. Let's go.
=> END

~ s4_locker
Cyrus Rowe: A priest's spare robes. Nobody looks twice at a priest.
do Campaign.give_item("cyrus", "priest_robes")
Cyrus Rowe: Well - nobody but another priest.
=> END

~ s4_checkpoint
Priest: Halt, brother. I don't know your face. Which chapel do you serve?
- The chapel of the Morning Bell.
	do Campaign.set_flag("stage4_passed")
	Priest: ...The Morning Bell. Of course. Go on, then.
- The big one. With the... roof.
	Priest: The big one with the roof. Guards!
- Does it matter?
	Priest: It matters a great deal to me. Guards!
=> END

~ s4_goal
Cyrus Rowe: Robes off, and out the back. Just another quiet night.
=> END

~ s5_goal
Cyrus Rowe: Out the window, and into the dark. They can keep their lamps.
=> END

~ s6_goal
Cyrus Rowe: One letter on the captain's desk, one sore stomach, and a supper he'll not forget.
=> END

~ s7_start
Cyrus Rowe: The whole camp's jumpy tonight. Somebody in a priest's robes could calm them down - a word here, a word there.
Cyrus Rowe: Not the chaplain, though. A priest knows a priest.
=> END

~ s7_goal
Cyrus Rowe: Through the checkpoint, and the camp none the wiser. Or at least none the calmer.
=> END
